# CODEOWNERS — added per /cso security review (v0.1.10).
#
# Required review on the paths with the largest blast radius:
#  - .github/   (CI workflows; can run arbitrary code in CI with GITHUB_TOKEN)
#  - install.sh (curl-pipe-bash entry point; reaches every user on next install)
#  - src/hook-entry.mjs and src/install.mjs (runs on user machines as their UID)
#  - src/memory-hook-entry.mjs (PreToolUse hook with permission decisions)
#  - skills/    (loaded by Claude Code as agent instructions)
#  - SECURITY.md (the threat model itself)
#
# Default ownership covers everything else.
# After adding this file, enable "Require review from Code Owners" on the
# main branch in the GitHub repo settings (Settings → Branches → Branch
# protection rules → main).

